{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/182162-how-do-geists-become-archetypes","id":182162,"title":"How do Geists become archetypes?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-27T12:57:23-07:00","id":182162,"title":"How do Geists become archetypes?","content":"Did the books ever talk about that? I was wondering if it happens in a specific place in the underworld. Do geist spirits have a common origin or do they just pop up everywhere? Are other underworld spirits aware of them and how they are born? Or is this one of those nobody knows things...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T14:23:50-07:00","id":182225,"title":"","content":"It's always struck me as &quot;a sufficiently old/powerful/angry ghost&quot; combining with a Death spirit (spirits as in &quot;from the Shadow, fought by Werewolves&quot; spirits) to become a geist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T03:48:30-07:00","id":182777,"title":"","content":"<br /> Well, it is one of those &quot;nobody really knows&quot; things. There is one eksample of a Geist being born out of two Ghosts who got into a fight near a River in the Underworld. They both fell in, and a single entity came out, the Geist Plenty.<br /> I'd purposely keep it vague, since that affords more mystery to the Geister. The &quot;Ghost eats multiple Death spirits, and becomes a Geist&quot;-thing, is not something I personally like, nor can really see happening, since there aren't really any Spirits in the Underworld, and I believe the process can only happen there. It also makes it seem alittle too 'simple', I'd say.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T11:37:17-07:00","id":183104,"title":"","content":"Where is the Geist Plenty mentioned?<br /> <br /> Hmm, maybe it has something to do with the rivers...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T12:14:45-07:00","id":183143,"title":"","content":"The writeup for Oppia in Chapter Five of Book of the Dead.<br /> <br /> Krob has confused the <i>thing</i> that pulled what would become Plenty under the surface of the River of Hate with another ghost; the creature merged with Euelpides' companion to become the geist.<br /> <br /> There's also the Traveler, from the same book, who is a ghost en rout to becoming a geist, who is attempting to get to a door deep in the Lower Mysteries, which goes to a place that is not a place; crossing that threshold, the Traveler's source claims, allows a ghost to become something that certainly sounds an awful lot like a geist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T13:14:57-07:00","id":183174,"title":"","content":"Ah. Not confused. Its just a long time I read the book. Yeah, the traveler certainly tries too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T21:40:38-07:00","id":184512,"title":"","content":"Doesn't the geist core book talk about the possibility of a ghost giving up its last anchor to replace it with a concept?<br /> <br /> So in your game, the Geist Martyrdom's Flame might be the result of a ghost eating a spirit, or a spirit eating a ghost, or a ghost achieving apotheosis through self-flanderization.<br /> <br /> For that matter, in second sight, it covers the topic of the loa, how as a group they might include ghosts and spirits, and maybe even ghosts of spirits and spirits that used to be ghosts.<br /> <br /> So perhaps Martyrdom's Flame might be the ghost of a faith spirit that retained some of its nature. <br /> <br /> For that matter, humans can become all sorts of things, like vampires and werewolves and mages, so some ghosts might just evolve into something more, like how Bloody Mary might be a ghost empowered by her legend achieving spirit like traits, or explain the ghost that has the entirety of the USA as his anchor that regains essence from killing people who almost died in wicked dead. Traveler's change would probably be seen as confirming this possible origin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T10:30:20-07:00","id":184942,"title":"","content":"Not the <i>last</i> - that's kept safeguarded by the keystone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T10:42:30-07:00","id":233015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/182162-how-do-geists-become-archetypes?p=184512#post184512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Doesn't the geist core book talk about the possibility of a ghost giving up its last anchor to replace it with a concept?</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue with this is that it's not supported elsewhere in the book. In fact, not a few pages later it talks about how a Geist is the result of a ghost that eats a spirit, or vice versa. A ghost that becomes more spirit-like. While &quot;replacing anchors with a concept&quot; might be a good way of looking at it, you've got ghosts that already have &quot;everyone who knows a certain knowledge&quot; as their Anchor (The founder of Cruac has anyone who knows Cruac as an anchor) or ghosts with obscenely large and unspecified anchors (Byakosh, the time vampire, has <i>the USA</i> as his anchor).<br /> <br /> Regardless, the one mechanical truth of Geists is that it takes Death 3 and Spirit 3 to manipulate their Patterns, meaning that they're Ghost-Spirits. They also had lives (considering Plumbing the Depths can tell you about it) so they aren't simply Spirits of Death.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/182162-how-do-geists-become-archetypes?p=184942#post184942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not the <i>last</i> - that's kept safeguarded by the keystone.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with this is that it's outright contradicted by the rest of the book. None of the Geists have an Anchor listed at all, and they're not shown as being tied to their Anchors. They also aren't limited to staying in the real world, like an anchored ghost would be: Plenty rules Oppia, while The Family Man goes to-and-fro between the Underworld and the world of the living. Likewise, ghosts in the Underworld don't have anchors, but the sidebar talking about Spirits eating ghosts to become Geists makes mention of how there are doorways that open between Underworld and Shadow. <br /> <br /> More than that, none of the Unfettered Geists are written up as having Keystones, either, and the Keystones seem to have come from the incident that created the Bound as often as they do from the Geist. The one that most comes to mind is La Diabla Blanca, who's Keystone isn't from her Geist but instead was one of the bandanna worn by the gang members who killed her.<br /> <br /> While in most WoD books I'd chalk this up to intentionally conflicting origin stories, in this case it just feels like Geist's poor editing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T11:35:01-07:00","id":233076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/182162-how-do-geists-become-archetypes?p=233015#post233015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with this is that it's outright contradicted by the rest of the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. The problem is that &quot;anchors&quot; is an ambiguous term that Geist appears to use in both the pre- and post-GMC senses of &quot;the discrete elements that tie a ghost to the mortal sphere upon their creation&quot; and &quot;the emotional context that forms the basis of a ghost's ties to the mortal world.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T12:21:33-07:00","id":233136,"title":"","content":"The keystone is described as the geist giving a physical token of its last anchor to the Sin-Eater for safekeeping, and that geists are terrified of loosing their last one. Any other anchors they may have are given up in exchange for more archetypal power, or subsumed beneath their bizarre new nature. No examples are given as to what those anchors are because their supposed to be a resolution that is hidden and difficult to discover, and entirely in the hands of the storyteller as to how trying to find it will work. [Also as a side note: affecting the pattern of Astral figments requires Mind + Spirit, and affecting GM angels is, I believe, Prime + Spirit. Unless all of these beings are part spirit, it may just be the arcana for messing with not-easily-categorized ephemera.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T12:40:53-07:00","id":233155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/182162-how-do-geists-become-archetypes?p=233136#post233136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The keystone is described as the geist giving a physical token of its last anchor to the Sin-Eater for safekeeping, and that geists are terrified of loosing their last one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because I made this error until my last reread of the Geist corebook: the keystone isn't specifically a token of the geist's last anchor - the &quot;last anchor&quot; specification is for ghosts being bound into fetters. The keystone is variously described as the core of the geist's history/identity, a symbol of the Bargain, and a safeguard against losing the geist's last anchor, but it's not necessarily tied to a specific aspect of the geist's connection to the land of the living.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unless all of these beings are part spirit, it may just be the arcana for messing with not-easily-categorized ephemera.] </div> </div> </div>It being in the makeup of Outer Channel and Summon Chthonian suggests this is indeed the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:24:58-07:00","id":233562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/182162-how-do-geists-become-archetypes?p=233076#post233076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. The problem is that &quot;anchors&quot; is an ambiguous term that Geist appears to use in both the pre- and post-GMC senses of &quot;the discrete elements that tie a ghost to the mortal sphere upon their creation&quot; and &quot;the emotional context that forms the basis of a ghost's ties to the mortal world.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Geist was out the door before GMC was even a twinkle in anyone's eye. Anchors is not an ambiguous term, and other write ups for ghosts include the anchors. And again, the Keystones often come from the Sin-eaters themselves, not the Geist. Likewise, the Geists ignore all the rules for ghosts with Anchors.<br /> <br /> There's literally no possible way within the confines of either the mechanics or the fluff to have an Anchor. Only one paragraph supports the idea, and all the rest ignore it completely, instead focusing on the concept of a ghost that was eaten by a spirit, or at the least became more like a Spirit through some manner other than it's Anchors.<br /> <br /> The fact of the matter is that there <i>is</i> no explanation of how the Geist becomes archetypal, only contradictory pieces of fluff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:53:06-07:00","id":233596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/182162-how-do-geists-become-archetypes?p=233562#post233562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Geist was out the door before GMC was even a twinkle in anyone's eye.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am aware of this, having written an entire term paper on the game a couple months before GMC came out. I'm also aware that literally every fetter writeup describes the context that made the object an anchor of the ghost whose story it describes and thus that the 2e concept of anchors was not pulled out of a hat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anchors is not an ambiguous term, and other write ups for ghosts include the anchors. </div> </div> </div>You will notice that taking this stance results in the thoroughly useless question of what allows ghosts who have been banished to the Underworld to return in the old mechanics without developing One Step Behind or similar means of circumventing the geographical limitations of an anchor. Meanwhile, &quot;anchors often have an emotional context&quot; goes clear back to WoD Core and extends past and partially through 1e Geist into GMC's ghost-particular Ephemeral Being mechanics - note the storytelling advice for Underworld ghosts, the requirements of the Pass On ceremony, and the implications of GMC's decreased emphasis on ghost-resolution.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And again, the Keystones often come from the Sin-eaters themselves, not the Geist. </div> </div> </div>Your evidence for this is literally composed solely of La Diabla Blanca's writeup and possibly a particular interpretation of Michael bin Michael's.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Likewise, the Geists ignore all the rules for ghosts with Anchors. </div> </div> </div>Yup. And the True Fae ignore the Lost's requirement of needing to have an idea of where they're going to navigate to anywhere on Earth through the Hedge, and the Strix ignore the Kindred's need for Touchstones to maintain non-torpor.<br /> <br /> It's almost as if this is a recurring element of the World of Darkness's handling of humanlike and non-humanlike supernaturals and their respective ability to maintain activity on Earth and in stranger spheres.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's literally no possible way within the confines of either the mechanics or the fluff to have an Anchor. Only one paragraph supports the idea, and all the rest ignore it completely, instead focusing on the concept of a ghost that was eaten by a spirit, or at the least became more like a Spirit through some manner other than it's Anchors. </div> </div> </div>One sidebar speculatively addressing a similarity doesn't outweigh a corebook paragraph that has greater thematic resonance with the notion of ghosts as creatures that cling to attachments to the world in the form of anchors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The fact of the matter is that there <i>is</i> no explanation of how the Geist becomes archetypal, only contradictory pieces of fluff. </div> </div> </div>Multiple-choice backstory's funny like that, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T19:28:13-07:00","id":233617,"title":"","content":"I never said anchors don't have emotional context. <br /> And whether it's &quot;solely&quot; from one character or not, there's still a black and white example of the opposite of what you said. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yup. And the True Fae ignore the Lost's requirement of needing to have an idea of where they're going to navigate to anywhere on Earth through the Hedge, and the Strix ignore the Kindred's need for Touchstones to maintain non-torpor. </div> </div> </div>So your argument is that Geists have anchors because they... ignore all rules for ghosts with anchors? That's kind of a terrible argument. And something that important, don't you think it would be mentioned more than once?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One sidebar speculatively addressing a similarity doesn't outweigh a corebook paragraph that has greater thematic resonance with the notion of ghosts as creatures that cling to attachments to the world in the form of anchors. </div> </div> </div> No, but every other depiction of how Geists become Geists follows that sidebar, not the paragraph saying they replace all but one of their anchors. The Traveling Man doesn't have an anchor.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You will notice that taking this stance results in the thoroughly useless question of what allows ghosts who have been banished to the Underworld to return in the old mechanics without developing One Step Behind or similar means of circumventing the geographical limitations of an anchor. </div> </div> </div>Another thing that can be chalked up to the Geist corebook's lack of focus or direction. At least in <i>Book of the Dead</i> things actually acknowledge Anchors. Crash the Gates for instance creates an Anchor for the released Ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:07:24-07:00","id":233665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/182162-how-do-geists-become-archetypes?p=233617#post233617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So your argument is that Geists have anchors because they... ignore all rules for ghosts with anchors? That's kind of a terrible argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good thing it's not my argument, then!<br /> <br /> Speculation on the nature of the Unfettered goes a number of ways, but must necessarily address the matter of their behaving like ghosts in a number of ways while lacking a number of qualities ghosts possess, such as Integrity/Morality and the mobility constraints of anchors. &quot;They've formed a metaphysical organ that they essentially treat as an innate version of the conditions that allow them to move freely across the border of life and death&quot; is one such piece of speculation, and &quot;something that is not a ghost subsumed a ghost and is using its memories as the basis for a personality or agenda or connection to mortality&quot; is another. Neither of them is especially provable outside the context of individual games, because geister and the Underworld tend to be full of misdirection and false leads and the origins of geister in general seem to be so diverse as to suggest a broader commonality than can be readily discerned beyond &quot;ghosts and/or the Underworld or something behind them are probably involved.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Unfettered act like ghosts in some ways and act like alien inhuman entities whose psychology-as-such is partially fixated on their nature as reflection of a nonhuman concept in others - ghosts without anchors-as-in-obsessions-with-the-living-world tend to have either passed on or gotten caught up in one of the Lower Mysteries that doesn't concern itself with lasting residence on Earth, while geister suffer neither of these fates but retain the ability to move among the living and thus either have at least one anchor or have otherwise transcended the need for anchors in a fashion that has not obliterated their ephemeral form.<br /> <br /> The <i>how</i> of it is immaterial to the fact that it <i>is</i>, and given that Geist is a game that deals primarily with ghosts and the Underworld I find it prudent to focus more on theories that engage with those aspects of the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, but every other depiction of how Geists become Geists follows that sidebar, not the paragraph saying they replace all but one of their anchors. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Every other depiction&quot; here being &quot;the rules for affecting unBound geister with the Arcana,&quot; &quot;the existence of unkeyed Avernian Gates into Shadow,&quot; and nothing else. A thing in an Underworld river is not a spirit of the Shadow unless it's been severely displaced. A door to a place that is not a place deep in the Underworld is not a spirit of the Shadow. <i>Being an ex-leader of a South American death squad who died peacefully in his sleep</i> is not a spirit of the Shadow.<br /> <br /> The description on page 20 of the corebook concerning what anchors are is resonant with the notion of ghosts as becoming more alien the deeper into the Underworld and the further they move from humanity (and their being drawn further into the Underworld with more time isolated from humanity). Geister being &quot;for all intents and purposes&quot; ghosts-hybridized-with-spirits is 1) specifically called out as mysterious and irrelevant and 2) a thing that writers have mentioned is not liable to receive further emphasis in a hypothetical future release, and for these and other reasons I don't lend the notion much credence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Traveling Man doesn't have an anchor. </div> </div> </div>The Traveler is a ghost in the Underworld. That he is not a geist is kind of the entire point of him as a character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T22:50:08-07:00","id":233883,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Traveler is a ghost in the Underworld. That he is not a geist is kind of the entire point of him as a character. </div> </div> </div> That he's <i>becoming</i> one is the entire point of the character.<br /> <br /> Also, do you intentionally couch all your talk in as confusing and circuitous language as possible or is it just a personality quirk? <br /> <br /> Every other depiction of Geists would be everything throughout the rest of the book, the Traveler's story, the way that Geists are never ever again mentioned in connection to anchors... the mentions in <i>Book of the Dead</i> about how ghosts might find themselves in the Shadow, or Spirits might find themselves in the Underworld...<br /> <br /> You've got literally one mention to support your theory and there are several more that contradict it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Speculation on the nature of the Unfettered goes a number of ways, but must necessarily address the matter of their behaving like ghosts in a number of ways while lacking a number of qualities ghosts possess, such as Integrity/Morality and the mobility constraints of anchors. </div> </div> </div>No, it mustn't. Geists are presented as fundamentally different than ghosts in all respects. They even have a quality called &quot;Not Quite Ghosts&quot;. The Keystone is never called out as an anchor.<br /> </span><br /> </span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}